All solid convex polygons are homeomorphic to each other. A solid convex polygon, being a 2D convex set with a boundary, is topologically equivalent to a closed disk. This is because convexity ensures the shape is simply connected and its boundary is a simple closed curve (homeomorphic to a circle). Since all disks (regardless of their boundary's polygonal structure) are homeomorphic, every solid convex polygon is homeomorphic to the 2D disk. 

